ch line continues on its own country’s national statistics, marked as such in its panel. The United States’ own figures fall after the 2022 peak, to 13.7 per 100,000 in 2024.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="mt-20"><h3 class="font-display m-0 text-[26px] font-semibold text-foreground">And in the crime record?</h3><div class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-14 xl:grid-cols-3"><div><div><span class="font-display block text-4xl font-semibold text-foreground">905</span><span class="body-copy mt-3 block text-[18px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/80">DHS human trafficking arrests in HSI-led operations around the 2026 World Cup, and 180 trafficking victims recovered — 30 of them children. Arrests count activity, and DHS publishes no breakdown of eventual charges; the 180 recovered is the outcome.</span><a href="https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/07/29/dhs-highlights-successful-arrests-and-rescues-crackdown-human-trafficking-during" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="mt-3 inline-block text-[15px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">DHS, 29 July 2026</a></div></div><div><div><span class="font-display block text-4xl font-semibold text-foreground">51% below</span><span class="body-copy mt-3 block text-[18px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/80">its 1997 peak: criminal arrests fell from 15.28 million that year to 7.52 million in 2024. Civil immigration arrests, counted by a different agency on a different calendar, moved the other way.</span><a href="/data/crime" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="mt-3 inline-block text-[15px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">Crime — the finding</a></div></div><div><div><span class="font-display block text-4xl font-semibold text-foreground">Down 9.3%</span><span class="body-copy mt-3 block text-[18px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/80">in violent crime in 2025 \u2014 the largest year-to-year decline since the FBI began estimating in 1936. Murder fell 18.1%, to the lowest rate ever recorded.</span><a href="https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/fbi-releases-2025-reported-crimes-in-the-nation-statistics" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="mt-3 inline-block text-[15px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">FBI, 2025 Reported Crimes in the Nation</a></div></div></div></div><div class="mt-16 border-l-2 border-foreground pl-5"><p class="body-copy measure m-0 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">Did any of that come from the systems in the section above? Nothing here measures it. The procurement register records what was bought, deployed and accredited — vendor, geography, workload, maturity — and carries no field for whether crime rose or fell anywhere a system landed. No record in this archive connects the two, and this archive does not claim they are connected.</p><p class="body-copy measure mt-5 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">The fall is also a police measure. The Bureau of Justice Statistics’ victimisation survey does not show the same recovery — 23.3 violent victimisations per 1,000 people in 2024 against 16.5 in 2021 — and about 48% of them were reported to police at all.<!-- --> <a href="https://bjs.ojp.gov/library/publications/nations-two-crime-measures-2015-2024" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">BJS, The Nation’s Two Crime Measures</a></p></div><div class="mt-12 border-t border-edge/60 pt-8 "><dl class="m-0 flex flex-col gap-5"><div class="flex flex-col gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline"><dt class="font-display shrink-0 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted sm:w-[104px]">Concepts</dt><dd class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-5 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#co-occurrence-is-not-cause" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Co-occurrence is not cause</a><a href="/concepts#low-number-may-mean-low-counting" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">A low number may mean low counting</a><a href="/concepts#us-rose-against-the-trend" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">The US rose against the trend</a><a href="/concepts#the-fentanyl-reversal" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">The fentanyl reversal</a><a href="/concepts#prescribing-is-not-prevalence" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Prescribing is not prevalence</a></dd></div></dl></div></div><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4"><a href="/data" class="inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground px-6 text-[17px] font-medium text-background">Go to all research</a><a href="/data/public-health" class="inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground/[0.07] px-6 text-[17px] hover:bg-foreground/[0.12]">Public health</a><a href="/data/crime" class="inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground/[0.07] px-6 text-[17px] hover:bg-foreground/[0.12]">Crime</a><button type="button" class="text-[16px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed">How to read the research</button></div></div></section><section id="neurotechnology" class="relative isolate overflow-hidden scroll-mt-24"><div data-motif="lattice" aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute z-0 select-none overflow-hidden inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-[58%] sm:inset-0 sm:h-auto text-foreground opacity-[0.14] dark:opacity-[0.11] [-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,transparent_0%,black_34%)] [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,transparent_0%,black_34%)] [--motif-p:0]"><svg viewBox="0 0 1200 620" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true" class="h-full w-full [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] [&amp;_circle]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] [&amp;_rect]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] origin-[50%_50%] scale-[2.0] sm:scale-[1.3] lg:scale-[0.88]"><circle cx="170" cy="310" r="9" opacity="0.85"></circle><g class="[stroke-dashoffset:calc(1_-_min(1,var(--motif-p)_*_2.1))]"><path d="M170 310 C 300 310, 340 220, 470 210" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path><path d="M170 310 C 300 310, 340 400, 470 415" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path></g><g opacity="0.85" class="[stroke-dashoffset:calc(1_-_min(1,max(0,var(--motif-p)_-_0.22)_*_2.1))]"><path d="M470 210 C 600 200, 640 120, 790 110" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path><path d="M470 210 C 610 230, 660 290, 800 285" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path><path d="M470 415 C 600 400, 640 352, 790 345" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path><path d="M470 415 C 610 425, 650 500, 800 505" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path></g><g opacity="0.70" class="[stroke-dashoffset:calc(1_-_min(1,max(0,var(--motif-p)_-_0.44)_*_2.4))]"><path d="M790 110 L1010 92" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path><path d="M800 285 L1030 300" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path><path d="M790 345 L1010 358" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path><path d="M800 505 L1020 530" pathLength="1" stroke-dasharray="1"></path></g><g class="[opacity:calc(max(0,var(--motif-p)_-_0.62)_*_2.4)]"><circle cx="1010" cy="92" r="5"></circle><circle cx="1030" cy="300" r="5"></circle><circle cx="1010" cy="358" r="5"></circle><circle cx="1020" cy="530" r="5"></circle></g></svg></div><div class="relative z-10 w-full px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:px-[200px]"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-1.5 w-6 shrink-0 bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="m-0 font-display text-[20px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-foreground">Concepts</p></div><h2 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.25] text-foreground sm:text-[34px]">What does the record actually establish?</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] text-muted">40<!-- --> concepts · <!-- -->30<!-- --> dated sources, the earliest from <!-- -->1888<!-- --> · <!-- -->19<!-- --> carry a public link</p><div class="mt-12"><p class="body-copy measure text-[24px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">What the record establishes, what it does not, and what could be built instead. The process this archive names for producing these effects deliberately is<!-- --> <a href="/glossary/neuro-engagement" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">neuro-engagement</a>.</p><div class="mt-12"><div><div class="relative" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Concepts"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="flex -ml-4"><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">documented · experience</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.3] text-foreground sm:text-[26px]">Your house is not haunted</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">Your house is not haunted, and that is a finding rather than a reassurance. In 2014 Olaf Blanke&#x27;s group manufactured the feeling of a presence in healthy people: a blindfolded participant moved a lever, a robot reproduced the movement against their back, and a half-second delay was enough that one in three felt someone standing behind them — two asked for the experiment to stop. Nobody was ever in the room with them. What this record describes is that effect imposed rather than induced: phantom sensations across every sense, and visuals reproducing what a haunting is supposed to look like. The terror is the mechanism — a household driven outside will accept help from whoever is waiting, and what this record says waits there is a facilitator of Zersetzung tactics and a suggestion of euthanasia.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#what-produces-the-feeling" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Read the concept<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">structural · surveillance</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.3] text-foreground sm:text-[26px]">Who could refuse a system that saved their child?</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">Imagine the terms inverted: you are told whenever you are observed, harassment is a crime rather than a method, and law enforcement is paid for harm that did not happen rather than arrests that did. Now the hard case: someone on a registry is present where children are, and the system flags it in seconds rather than after a report — an automation raises it, a person reviews it, a person decides. The intervention is closer to social work than policing; the individual is steered away, no crime occurs, and a child goes home that afternoon never knowing there was an afternoon to survive. The family is told a harm was prevented, and invited to review the service. What they feel is relief so total it forecloses argument, and that is the finding: a system justified by the worst thing that could happen to your child cannot be argued with by anyone who loves a child.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#prevention-as-the-product" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Read the concept<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">structural · surveillance</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.3] text-foreground sm:text-[26px]">Why does the camera on your door not answer to you?</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">A doorbell camera watches your street and answers to its manufacturer. You can look at what it recorded; you do not hold it, and you cannot say who else can. The proposal here is narrower than a privacy argument and harder to dismiss: give a citizen their own eyesight — one recording that belongs to the person the way a body camera belongs to an officer. The procurement record gives that proposal an uncomfortable shape. 9bn across 27 awards, and 93 deployments in 21 of the 35 geographies tracked.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#whose-eyesight-is-it" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Read the concept<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">documented · neurotech</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.3] text-foreground sm:text-[26px]">Why did legislatures write laws for neural data?</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">Legislatures rarely move early. On neural data, three of them did. Colorado passed HB24-1058 in 2024, amending its consumer privacy act to require express consent before neural data is collected or used, separate consent or an opt-out before it goes to a third party, and a route for a person to have it deleted. California did the same through SB 1223, folding neural data into the categories its privacy act treats as sensitive. Montana went further from a different direction, adding neural data to its genetic information privacy act, effective October 2025.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#law-for-neural-data" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Read the concept<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">documented · coercion</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.3] text-foreground sm:text-[26px]">Organised covert harassment of individuals is established fact</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">Not a theory, and not confined to states. Seven decided or settled cases in this record describe sustained, deniable targeting of named people — by police forces and by corporations. Two further entries are included as context and as a contested case, and are labelled as such rather than counted alongside these.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#organised-harassment-is-fact" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Read the concept<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">documented · neurotech</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.3] text-foreground sm:text-[26px]">Can a machine read what you are thinking?</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">Partly, under conditions that are worth stating precisely. In May 2023 Jerry Tang and Alexander Huth published a semantic decoder in Nature Neuroscience that reconstructed continuous language from non-invasive brain recordings. A person lay in an fMRI scanner; a transformer model turned the blood-flow signal into text that captured the gist of what they were hearing or imagining, matching the intended meaning roughly half the time. It is a real result and it was replicated in the paper across participants. The conditions are as important as the finding.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#can-a-machine-read-thought" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Read the concept<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">documented · record</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.3] text-foreground sm:text-[26px]">Why isn&#x27;t any of this in the news?</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">The usual assumption is that silence means suppression. There is a duller explanation with far better evidence behind it, and anyone reasoning about an absence of coverage should meet it first. Local journalism in the United States has collapsed. Northwestern&#x27;s Medill School has tracked it annually; its 2025 State of Local News report counts nearly 3,500 newspapers gone since 2005 — close to forty per cent of all local papers in the country — with 136 lost in the last year alone. Two hundred and thirteen counties now have no local news source of any kind.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#why-isnt-this-in-the-news" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Read the concept<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div></div></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5"><button type="button" aria-label="Previous slide" disabled="" class="z-10 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-background text-muted transition-colors hover:text-foreground disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-40 left-1 top-1/2 static mr-1 h-11 w-11 translate-y-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-left h-4 w-4"><path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"></path><path d="M19 12H5"></path></svg></button><button type="button" aria-label="Next slide" disabled="" class="z-10 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-background text-muted transition-colors hover:text-foreground disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-40 right-1 top-1/2 static mr-2 h-11 w-11 translate-y-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right h-4 w-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 1 of 7" aria-current="true" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-7 bg-foreground"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 2 of 7" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 3 of 7" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 4 of 7" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 5 of 7" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 6 of 7" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 7 of 7" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><span class="ml-2 text-[15px] text-muted">1<!-- --> / <!-- -->7</span></div></div></div></div><div class="mt-12 border-t border-edge/60 pt-8 "><dl class="m-0 flex flex-col gap-5"><div class="flex flex-col gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline"><dt class="font-display shrink-0 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted sm:w-[104px]">Glossary</dt><dd class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-5 gap-y-2"><a href="/glossary/neuro-engagement" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Neuro-engagement</a><a href="/glossary/phantom-sensations" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Phantom sensations</a><a href="/glossary/perceptual-set" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Perceptual set</a><a href="/glossary/cognitive-liberty" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Cognitive liberty</a></dd></div></dl></div></div><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4"><a href="/concepts" class="inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground px-6 text-[17px] font-medium text-background">Go to the concepts</a><button type="button" class="text-[16px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed">How to read this archive</button></div></div></section><section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden"><div data-motif="recede" aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute z-0 select-none overflow-hidden inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-[58%] sm:inset-0 sm:h-auto text-foreground opacity-[0.14] dark:opacity-[0.11] [-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,transparent_0%,black_34%)] [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,transparent_0%,black_34%)] [--motif-p:0]"><svg viewBox="0 0 1200 620" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" aria-hidden="true" class="h-full w-full [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] [&amp;_circle]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] [&amp;_rect]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] origin-[50%_100%] scale-[2.0] sm:scale-[1.3] lg:scale-[0.88]"><g class="[transform-box:fill-box] origin-bottom [transform:scale(calc(1_+_var(--motif-p)_*_0.22))]"><path d="M600 40 L-120 600"></path><path d="M600 40 L60 600" opacity="0.85"></path><path d="M600 40 L260 600" opacity="0.70"></path><path d="M600 40 L440 600" opacity="0.70"></path><path d="M600 40 L600 600" opacity="0.70"></path><path d="M600 40 L760 600" opacity="0.70"></path><path d="M600 40 L940 600" opacity="0.70"></path><path d="M600 40 L1140 600" opacity="0.85"></path><path d="M600 40 L1320 600"></path><path d="M-120 600 L1320 600"></path><path d="M170 420 L1030 420" opacity="0.70"></path><path d="M360 268 L840 268" opacity="0.70"></path><path d="M470 168 L730 168" opacity="0.70"></path></g></svg></div><div class="relative z-10 w-full px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:px-[200px]"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-1.5 w-6 shrink-0 bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="m-0 font-display text-[20px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-foreground">Glossary</p></div><h2 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.25] text-foreground sm:text-[34px]">What do these words actually mean?</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] text-muted">45 terms · pronunciation, definition, and every entry in the record that uses them</p><div class="mt-12"><p class="body-copy measure text-[24px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">Some of these name something documented and some name something claimed, and telling them apart is most of the work. A reader who cannot say which is which cannot evaluate anything else on this page — so the order below puts a historically documented tactic first, and sets a published physical effect directly beside the claim that resembles it.</p><div class="mt-12"><div><div class="relative" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Glossary terms"><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="flex -ml-4"><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">tsair·ZET·soong</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground sm:text-4xl">Zersetzung tactics</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">” A specific, documented strategy of covert psychological attrition — disruption, gaslighting, isolation, and manufactured setbacks — used to quietly destabilize and discredit a targeted person without overt force; developed and used by the East German Stasi. Where gang stalking is a vernacular term for the general pattern, Zersetzung is a defined, historically documented methodology. In this work, such tactics are applied and amplified through neuro-technology.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/glossary/zersetzung-tactics" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Full definition and every entry that uses it<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">gang STAWK·ing</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground sm:text-4xl">Gang stalking</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">A vernacular term — originating within the targeted-individual community — for the coordinated surveillance and harassment of a single individual by multiple people acting in concert. It names the reported pattern of coordinated harassment, as distinct from a specific documented methodology such as Zersetzung tactics. Most often reported by those who identify as targeted individuals.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/glossary/gang-stalking" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Full definition and every entry that uses it<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">also “Frey effect”</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground sm:text-4xl">microwave auditory effect</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">A documented phenomenon in which pulsed microwave or radio-frequency energy is perceived as clicks, buzzes, or hums that seem to originate inside the head, with no external sound. First reported by scientist Allan H. Frey in 1961, it arises through thermoelastic expansion — the pulsed energy causes rapid, minute heating of head tissue, generating a tiny pressure wave that the inner ear detects as sound.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/glossary/microwave-auditory-effect" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Full definition and every entry that uses it<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">voyss·too·skuhl · synthetic telepathy</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground sm:text-4xl">Voice-to-skull (V2K)</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">A claimed method of transmitting brain–computer interface data — signals sent to the brain — remotely and with no implanted device, such that a person perceives audible speech or sound inside the head with no external acoustic source.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/glossary/voice-to-skull" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Full definition and every entry that uses it<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">per·SEP·choo·uhl set, noun</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground sm:text-4xl">perceptual set</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">A perceptual set is a tendency to perceive or notice some aspects of the available sensory data and ignore others. It is heavily influenced by expectations, past experience, and context. If an object is completely outside a person&#x27;s prior experience (their “set”), they may not select it for conscious attention — effectively rendering it “invisible” to the mind&#x27;s eye, even if the retinas physically register it.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/glossary/perceptual-set" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Full definition and every entry that uses it<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-full"><article class="flex flex-col pr-0 sm:pr-10 min-h-[260px] md:min-h-[300px]"><p class="m-0 font-display text-[16px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">Glossary</p><h3 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground sm:text-4xl">cognitive liberty</h3><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-start py-6"><p class="m-0 font-serif text-[20px] leading-[1.6] text-foreground sm:text-[22px] sm:leading-[1.55]">An evolving concept asserting the fundamental right of an individual to sovereignty over their own mind and consciousness. It extends the traditional right to “freedom of thought” to address challenges raised by neuroscience and technology — brain–computer interfaces that can read from or write to the brain, neuro-enhancements that alter memory or attention, and AI systems that can exploit cognitive biases, micro-target persuasion, or reconstruct thoughts from brain data.</p></div><div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2"><a href="/glossary/cognitive-liberty" class="ml-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[16px] text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Full definition and every entry that uses it<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></article></div></div></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5"><button type="button" aria-label="Previous slide" disabled="" class="z-10 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-background text-muted transition-colors hover:text-foreground disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-40 left-1 top-1/2 static mr-1 h-11 w-11 translate-y-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-left h-4 w-4"><path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"></path><path d="M19 12H5"></path></svg></button><button type="button" aria-label="Next slide" disabled="" class="z-10 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-background text-muted transition-colors hover:text-foreground disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-40 right-1 top-1/2 static mr-2 h-11 w-11 translate-y-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right h-4 w-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 1 of 6" aria-current="true" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-7 bg-foreground"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 2 of 6" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 3 of 6" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 4 of 6" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 5 of 6" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><button type="button" aria-label="Show 6 of 6" aria-current="false" class="px-1 py-3"><span class="block h-1.5 transition-all w-2.5 bg-foreground/20"></span></button><span class="ml-2 text-[15px] text-muted">1<!-- --> / <!-- -->6</span></div></div></div></div><div class="mt-12 border-t border-edge/60 pt-8 "><dl class="m-0 flex flex-col gap-5"><div class="flex flex-col gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline"><dt class="font-display shrink-0 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted sm:w-[104px]">Concepts</dt><dd class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-5 gap-y-2"><a href="/concepts#the-neurotech-bullhorn" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">What is the neurotech bullhorn?</a><a href="/concepts#can-you-record-it" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Can you record it?</a><a href="/concepts#organised-harassment-is-fact" class="text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground">Organised covert harassment is established fact</a></dd></div></dl></div></div><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4"><a href="/glossary" class="inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground px-6 text-[17px] font-medium text-background">Go to the glossary</a></div></div></section><section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden"><div data-motif="room" aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute z-0 select-none overflow-hidden inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-[58%] sm:inset-0 sm:h-auto text-foreground opacity-[0.14] dark:opacity-[0.11] [-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,transparent_0%,black_34%)] [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,transparent_0%,black_34%)] [--motif-p:0]"><svg viewBox="0 0 1200 620" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true" class="h-full w-full [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] [&amp;_circle]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] [&amp;_rect]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke] origin-[50%_50%] scale-[2.0] sm:scale-[1.3] lg:scale-[0.88]"><g class="[transform:translateY(calc(var(--motif-p)_*_-26px))]"><path d="M120 96 L740 40 L740 470"></path><path d="M740 40 L1180 96"></path></g><g class="[transform:translateY(calc(var(--motif-p)_*_-54px))]"><path d="M740 470 L120 528"></path><path d="M740 470 L1180 528"></path><path d="M150 190 L520 168 L520 372 L150 356 Z"></path><path d="M170 206 L502 186 L502 356 L170 342 Z" opacity="0.70"></path></g><g class="[transform:translateY(calc(var(--motif-p)_*_-92px))]"><path d="M96 428 L560 404 L560 462 L96 490 Z"></path><path d="M330 416 L330 476" opacity="0.70"></path></g></svg></div><div class="relative z-10 w-full px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:px-[200px]"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-1.5 w-6 shrink-0 bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="m-0 font-display text-[20px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-foreground">Contribute</p></div><h2 class="font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.25] text-foreground sm:text-[34px]">What can you do?</h2><div class="mt-12"><p class="body-copy measure text-[24px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">The most important thing is also the hardest to hold on to: you are not communicating with the spirit world, and you are not communicating with extraterrestrials. Nothing in this archive points anywhere but at people — people with equipment, working for organisations, for reasons that are ordinary even when what they do is not.</p><div class="mt-14 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-12 xl:grid-cols-3"><div><h3 class="font-display m-0 text-[21px] font-semibold text-foreground">Meet the documented explanations first</h3><p class="body-copy mt-2 text-[18px] text-foreground/85">A feeling of presence can be produced in a laboratory in healthy people. Pulsed radio-frequency energy is genuinely heard as clicks inside the head — a published effect since 1961. Neither fact settles anything about what you have experienced. Both are worth knowing before the frightening explanations, because they are the ones that can be checked.</p><a href="/concepts#what-produces-the-feeling" class="mt-5 inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground/[0.07] px-4 text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-foreground/[0.12]">Your house is not haunted</a></div><div><h3 class="font-display m-0 text-[21px] font-semibold text-foreground">Protect your household</h3><p class="body-copy mt-2 text-[18px] text-foreground/85">Do not go outside looking for whoever you believe is speaking to you, and do not let anyone into your home. Do not answer or signal back. You cannot identify who you would be answering, and everything that follows from being wrong about that lands on your household. If you are frightened for your immediate safety, that is what emergency services are for — this site cannot see you or reach you, and the<!-- --> <button type="button" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-4" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed">safety notice</button> <!-- -->is where the people who can are listed.</p><a href="/concepts#can-you-record-it" class="mt-5 inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground/[0.07] px-4 text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-foreground/[0.12]">Can you record it?</a></div><div><h3 class="font-display m-0 text-[21px] font-semibold text-foreground">Keep your own record</h3><p class="body-copy mt-2 text-[18px] text-foreground/85">You do not need an account, permission, or this site to begin. Date every entry, note where you were, write what was said in the words it was said in, and leave it unsmoothed. That is the entire standard the archive in front of you was built to — and a contemporaneous record is what separates testimony from recollection later on.</p><a href="/concepts#no-column-for-you" class="mt-5 inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground/[0.07] px-4 text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-foreground/[0.12]">There is no column for you</a></div></div><p class="body-copy measure mt-16 text-[18px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/80">No news organisation has reported this. No agency has acknowledged it. Before reaching for what that might mean, there is a duller explanation with far better evidence behind it — nearly 3,500 American newspapers have closed since 2005, roughly forty per cent of the country’s local press.<!-- --> <a href="/concepts#why-isnt-this-in-the-news" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Why isn’t any of this in the news?</a></p><div class="mt-10 border-l-2 border-foreground pl-5"><p class="body-copy measure m-0 leading-relaxed text-foreground/85">A way to send your own transcripts to this archive is being built and is not finished. There is no sign-up yet, and there will not be one until it can receive an account safely. Until then the record you keep is yours, and it will still be yours when there is somewhere to send it.</p></div></div><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4"><button type="button" class="inline-flex h-12 items-center gap-2.5 rounded-md bg-foreground px-6 text-[17px] font-medium text-background"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-download" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"></polyline><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="15" y2="3"></line></svg>Corpus for AI</button><button type="button" class="text-[16px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed">Safety notice</button></div></div></section></main><footer class="mt-16 bg-foreground/[0.035]"><div class="w-full px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 lg:px-[100px]"><div class="grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4"><div><p class="font-display m-0 text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-foreground">Invisible Ships</p><p class="body-copy m-0 mt-3 max-w-xs text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted">A dated first-person record, and research from public sources beside it. Every figure resolves to a named source.</p></div><nav aria-label="The record"><p class="font-display m-0 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">The record</p><ul class="m-0 mt-4 list-none space-y-2.5 p-0"><li><a class="text-[14px] text-foreground/80 transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="/journal">Journal</a></li><li><a class="text-[14px] text-foreground/80 transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="/glossary">Glossary</a></li><li><a class="text-[14px] text-foreground/80 transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="/documents">Documents</a></li><li><a class="text-[14px] text-foregrou