ple in 2024 against 16.5 in 2021 — and about 48% of them were reported to police at all.\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://bjs.ojp.gov/library/publications/nations-two-crime-measures-2015-2024\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer noopener\",\"className\":\"text-foreground underline underline-offset-4\",\"children\":\"BJS, The Nation’s Two Crime Measures\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 border-t border-edge/60 pt-8 \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 flex flex-col gap-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"Concepts\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display shrink-0 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted sm:w-[104px]\",\"children\":\"Concepts\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-5 gap-y-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"/concepts#co-occurrence-is-not-cause\",{\"href\":\"/concepts#co-occurrence-is-not-cause\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"Co-occurrence is not cause\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/concepts#low-number-may-mean-low-counting\",{\"href\":\"/concepts#low-number-may-mean-low-counting\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"A low number may mean low counting\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/concepts#us-rose-against-the-trend\",{\"href\":\"/concepts#us-rose-against-the-trend\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"The US rose against the trend\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/concepts#the-fentanyl-reversal\",{\"href\":\"/concepts#the-fentanyl-reversal\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"The fentanyl reversal\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/concepts#prescribing-is-not-prevalence\",{\"href\":\"/concepts#prescribing-is-not-prevalence\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"Prescribing is not prevalence\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"a\",\"/data\",{\"href\":\"/data\",\"className\":\"inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground px-6 text-[17px] font-medium text-background\",\"children\":\"Go to all research\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/data/public-health\",{\"href\":\"/data/public-health\",\"className\":\"inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground/[0.07] px-6 text-[17px] hover:bg-foreground/[0.12]\",\"children\":\"Public health\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/data/crime\",{\"href\":\"/data/crime\",\"className\":\"inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground/[0.07] px-6 text-[17px] hover:bg-foreground/[0.12]\",\"children\":\"Crime\"}]],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"button\",null,{\"type\":\"button\",\"className\":\"text-[16px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground\",\"children\":\"How to read the research\"}]}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"id\":\"neurotechnology\",\"className\":\"relative isolate overflow-hidden scroll-mt-24\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"name\":\"lattice\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative z-10 w-full px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:px-[200px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"h-1.5 w-6 shrink-0 bg-accent\",\"aria-hidden\":true}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 font-display text-[20px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Concepts\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.25] text-foreground sm:text-[34px]\",\"children\":\"What does the record actually establish?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 text-[17px] text-muted\",\"children\":[40,\" concepts · \",30,\" dated sources, the earliest from \",1888,\" · \",19,\" carry a public link\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"body-copy measure text-[24px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/85\",\"children\":[\"What the record establishes, what it does not, and what could be built instead. The process this archive names for producing these effects deliberately is\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary/neuro-engagement\",\"className\":\"text-foreground underline underline-offset-4\",\"children\":\"neuro-engagement\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb\",null,{\"slides\":[{\"href\":\"/concepts#what-produces-the-feeling\",\"eyebrow\":\"documented · experience\",\"title\":\"Your house is not haunted\",\"body\":\"Your house is not haunted, and that is a finding rather than a reassurance. In 2014 Olaf Blanke's group manufactured the feeling of a presence in healthy people: a blindfolded participant moved a lever, a robot reproduced the movement against their back, and a half-second delay was enough that one in three felt someone standing behind them — two asked for the experiment to stop. Nobody was ever in the room with them. What this record describes is that effect imposed rather than induced: phantom sensations across every sense, and visuals reproducing what a haunting is supposed to look like. The terror is the mechanism — a household driven outside will accept help from whoever is waiting, and what this record says waits there is a facilitator of Zersetzung tactics and a suggestion of euthanasia.\",\"cta\":\"Read the concept\"},{\"href\":\"/concepts#prevention-as-the-product\",\"eyebrow\":\"structural · surveillance\",\"title\":\"Who could refuse a system that saved their child?\",\"body\":\"Imagine the terms inverted: you are told whenever you are observed, harassment is a crime rather than a method, and law enforcement is paid for harm that did not happen rather than arrests that did. Now the hard case: someone on a registry is present where children are, and the system flags it in seconds rather than after a report — an automation raises it, a person reviews it, a person decides. The intervention is closer to social work than policing; the individual is steered away, no crime occurs, and a child goes home that afternoon never knowing there was an afternoon to survive. The family is told a harm was prevented, and invited to review the service. What they feel is relief so total it forecloses argument, and that is the finding: a system justified by the worst thing that could happen to your child cannot be argued with by anyone who loves a child.\",\"cta\":\"Read the concept\"},{\"href\":\"/concepts#whose-eyesight-is-it\",\"eyebrow\":\"structural · surveillance\",\"title\":\"Why does the camera on your door not answer to you?\",\"body\":\"A doorbell camera watches your street and answers to its manufacturer. You can look at what it recorded; you do not hold it, and you cannot say who else can. The proposal here is narrower than a privacy argument and harder to dismiss: give a citizen their own eyesight — one recording that belongs to the person the way a body camera belongs to an officer. The procurement record gives that proposal an uncomfortable shape. 9bn across 27 awards, and 93 deployments in 21 of the 35 geographies tracked.\",\"cta\":\"Read the concept\"},{\"href\":\"/concepts#law-for-neural-data\",\"eyebrow\":\"documented · neurotech\",\"title\":\"Why did legislatures write laws for neural data?\",\"body\":\"Legislatures rarely move early. On neural data, three of them did. Colorado passed HB24-1058 in 2024, amending its consumer privacy act to require express consent before neural data is collected or used, separate consent or an opt-out before it goes to a third party, and a route for a person to have it deleted. California did the same through SB 1223, folding neural data into the categories its privacy act treats as sensitive. Montana went further from a different direction, adding neural data to its genetic information privacy act, effective October 2025.\",\"cta\":\"Read the concept\"},{\"href\":\"/concepts#organised-harassment-is-fact\",\"eyebrow\":\"documented · coercion\",\"title\":\"Organised covert harassment of individuals is established fact\",\"body\":\"Not a theory, and not confined to states. Seven decided or settled cases in this record describe sustained, deniable targeting of named people — by police forces and by corporations. Two further entries are included as context and as a contested case, and are labelled as such rather than counted alongside these.\",\"cta\":\"Read the concept\"},{\"href\":\"/concepts#can-a-machine-read-thought\",\"eyebrow\":\"documented · neurotech\",\"title\":\"Can a machine read what you are thinking?\",\"body\":\"Partly, under conditions that are worth stating precisely. In May 2023 Jerry Tang and Alexander Huth published a semantic decoder in Nature Neuroscience that reconstructed continuous language from non-invasive brain recordings. A person lay in an fMRI scanner; a transformer model turned the blood-flow signal into text that captured the gist of what they were hearing or imagining, matching the intended meaning roughly half the time. It is a real result and it was replicated in the paper across participants. The conditions are as important as the finding.\",\"cta\":\"Read the concept\"},{\"href\":\"/concepts#why-isnt-this-in-the-news\",\"eyebrow\":\"documented · record\",\"title\":\"Why isn't any of this in the news?\",\"body\":\"The usual assumption is that silence means suppression. There is a duller explanation with far better evidence behind it, and anyone reasoning about an absence of coverage should meet it first. Local journalism in the United States has collapsed. Northwestern's Medill School has tracked it annually; its 2025 State of Local News report counts nearly 3,500 newspapers gone since 2005 — close to forty per cent of all local papers in the country — with 136 lost in the last year alone. Two hundred and thirteen counties now have no local news source of any kind.\",\"cta\":\"Read the concept\"}],\"label\":\"Concepts\",\"titleSize\":\"heading\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 border-t border-edge/60 pt-8 \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 flex flex-col gap-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"Glossary\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display shrink-0 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted sm:w-[104px]\",\"children\":\"Glossary\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-5 gap-y-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"/glossary/neuro-engagement\",{\"href\":\"/glossary/neuro-engagement\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"Neuro-engagement\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/glossary/phantom-sensations\",{\"href\":\"/glossary/phantom-sensations\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"Phantom sensations\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/glossary/perceptual-set\",{\"href\":\"/glossary/perceptual-set\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"Perceptual set\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"/glossary/cognitive-liberty\",{\"href\":\"/glossary/cognitive-liberty\",\"className\":\"text-[17px] text-foreground underline decoration-foreground/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-foreground\",\"children\":\"Cognitive liberty\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"a\",\"/concepts\",{\"href\":\"/concepts\",\"className\":\"inline-flex h-12 items-center rounded-md bg-foreground px-6 text-[17px] font-medium text-background\",\"children\":\"Go to the concepts\"}]],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"button\",null,{\"type\":\"button\",\"className\":\"text-[16px] text-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground\",\"children\":\"How to read this archive\"}]}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"relative isolate overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"name\":\"recede\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative z-10 w-full px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:px-[200px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"h-1.5 w-6 shrink-0 bg-accent\",\"aria-hidden\":true}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 font-display text-[20px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Glossary\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display m-0 mt-3 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.25] text-foreground sm:text-[34px]\",\"children\":\"What do these words actually mean?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 text-[17px] text-muted\",\"children\":\"45 terms · pronunciation, definition, and every entry in the record that uses them\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"body-copy measure text-[24px] leading-relaxed text-foreground/85\",\"children\":\"Some of these name something documented and some name something claimed, and telling them apart is most of the work. A reader who cannot say which is which cannot evaluate anything else on this page — so the order below puts a historically documented tactic first, and sets a published physical effect directly beside the claim that resembles it.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb\",null,{\"slides\":[{\"href\":\"/glossary/zersetzung-tactics\",\"eyebrow\":\"tsair·ZET·soong\",\"title\":\"Zersetzung tactics\",\"body\":\"” A specific, documented strategy of covert psychological attrition — disruption, gaslighting, isolation, and manufactured setbacks — used to quietly destabilize and discredit a targeted person without overt force; developed and used by the East German Stasi. Where gang stalking is a vernacular term for the general pattern, Zersetzung is a defined, historically documented methodology. In this work, such tactics are applied and amplified through neuro-technology.\",\"cta\":\"Full definition and every entry that uses it\"},{\"href\":\"/glossary/gang-stalking\",\"eyebrow\":\"gang STAWK·ing\",\"title\":\"Gang stalking\",\"body\":\"A vernacular term — originating within the targeted-individual community — for the coordinated surveillance and harassment of a single individual by multiple people acting in concert. It names the reported pattern of coordinated harassment, as distinct from a specific documented methodology such as Zersetzung tactics. Most often reported by those who identify as targeted individuals.\",\"cta\":\"Full definition and every entry that uses it\"},{\"href\":\"/glossary/microwave-auditory-effect\",\"eyebrow\":\"also “Frey effect”\",\"title\":\"microwave auditory effect\",\"body\":\"A documented phenomenon in which pulsed microwave or radio-frequency energy is perceived as clicks, buzzes, or hums that seem to originate inside the head, with no external sound. First reported by scientist Allan H. Frey in 1961, it arises through thermoelastic expansion — the pulsed energy causes rapid, minute heating of head tissue, generating a tiny pressure wave that the inner ear detects as sound.\",\"cta\":\"Full definition and every entry that uses it\"},{\"href\":\"/glossary/voice-to-skull\",\"eyebrow\":\"voyss·too·skuhl · synthetic telepathy\",\"title\":\"Voice-to-skull (V2K)\",\"body\":\"A claimed method of transmitting brain–computer interface data — signals sent to the brain — remotely and with no implanted device, such that a person perceives audible speech or sound inside the head with no external acoustic source.\",\"cta\":\"Full definition and every entry that uses it\"},{\"href\":\"/glossary/perceptual-set\",\"eyebrow\":\"per·SEP·choo·uhl set, noun\",\"title\":\"perceptual set\",\"body\":\"A perceptual set is a tendency to perceive or notice some aspects of the available sensory data and ignore others. It is heavily influenced by expectations, past experience, and context. If an object is completely outside a person's prior experience (their “set”), they may not select it for conscious attention — effectively rendering it “invisible” to the mind's eye, even if the retinas physically register it.\",\"cta\":\"Full definition and every entry that uses it\"},{\"href\":\"/glossary/cognitive-liberty\",\"eyebrow\":\"Glossary\",\"title\":\"cognitive liberty\",\"body\":\"An evolving concept asserting the fundamental right of an individual to sovereignty over their own mind and consciousness. It extends the traditional right to “freedom of thought” to address challenges raised by neuroscience and technology — brain–computer interfaces that can read from or write to the brain, neuro-enhancements that alter memory or attention, and AI systems that can exploit cognitive biases, micro-target persuasion, or reconstruct thoughts from brain data.\",\"cta\":\"Full definition and every entry that uses it\"}],\"label\":\"Glossary terms\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 border-t border-edge/60 pt-8 \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"m-0 flex flex-col gap-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"Concepts\",{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"font-d